@namespace Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor

@* VariableExplorer with its state in the host's address bar, and no glue for the host to write.

   No @page and no @rendermode, the same as everything else here — but unlike everything else here
   this one does touch the URL, and that is the whole of what it adds. Mounting it is the host
   saying the explorer owns the query string; a host that wants to own it mounts VariableExplorer
   and keeps ExplorerUrlState. (Fhi.Metadata-zrcf4)

   Every parameter the explorer takes a value on is passed through, so mounting this costs a host
   nothing it would have had from mounting VariableExplorer itself. The seven Changed callbacks are
   deliberately not re-exposed: this component is what consumes them, and a host that wants them
   mounts the explorer with ExplorerUrlState instead. (Fhi.Metadata-l1f2s)

   No class names and no markup of its own: whatever the explorer draws is what a reader sees. *@

<VariableExplorer @bind-Search="_state.Search"
                  @bind-Filter="_state.Filter"
                  @bind-Sort="_state.Sort"
                  @bind-Direction="_state.Direction"
                  @bind-Page="_state.Page"
                  @bind-PageSize="_state.PageSize"
                  @bind-SelectedVariableId="_state.SelectedVariableId"
                  IsAuthenticated="@IsAuthenticated"
                  HeadingLevel="@HeadingLevel"
                  Language="@Language" />
